From 94a6c5141bce65c75d81fce90d8ad2225d295a01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:31:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix: lock on logind Lock and before sleep

`loginctl lock-session` emits Session.Lock on the session object, and a
suspend started outside the shell (systemctl suspend, a logind lid or
idle action) emits PrepareForSleep. The shell listened to neither, so
lock-session did nothing and lock-on-suspend only applied when the shell
itself suspended.

Follow both for the shell's own session, with logind as the sender. Lock
goes through PowerActions.lock_screen(). Before sleep a "sleep" delay
inhibitor is released once the lock screen is up (at most 3 s), or at
once when lock-on-suspend is off or the session is already locked.
Repeated requests are no-ops; Unlock is ignored.

